      "content": "Even if the pain feels similar to a past muscle strain, ignoring sudden radiation to the stomach and severe pain without medical supervision is extremely risky. You are also likely already taking two doses of ibuprofen if you have had any prior pain relief, which significantly increases your risk of dangerous stomach bleeds and kidney damage. Over-the-counter painkillers like ibuprofen should never be self-prescribed at high, repeated doses, regardless of your insurance status. Given the potential severity of conditions that mimic a bad back, please seek urgent medical advice to rule out life-threatening issues before attempting to manage this alone.",
